Z||000003||2birds||01-15-2000||10:30 PM||||I thought about paying to have mine done the last time, and the mechanic I checked with said his estimate manual listed the job at 8.1 hours.  I'm not sure what the exchange rate is nowadays, but that was around $400 in  US dollars.  I've seen rates as high as $65/hr at dealers, depending on the job.  My  clutch kit (RAM) cost $130 from summit (86 GT, V-6/5-speed).  I know the markup on parts is usually pretty high at a shop, since it will probably take more than 8.1 hours, though.  If you have access to the right tools, consider doing it yourself, or find someone that will install your parts.  It's basically the same as any small front drive GM.  ||||reg||1
